  "answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions with a focus on enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with a meeting on July 15th. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing ahead of schedule. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session scheduled for September 10th. The project is moving into the development phase next month, led by Omar Jensen, with UI enhancements planned for October. Budget updates indicate an approved budget of $2M from the executive board, with a specific training budget of $15,000 approved for coding teams and project managers. An adjustment to $550,000 was noted due to unforeseen expenses, likely referring to a specific component or phase. Partnership opportunities with TechInnovate for AI technology are being explored. A celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
